abel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Sources: Ole Miss RB Kewan Lacy to miss rest of season","description":"Ole Miss running back Kewan Lacy, who has one year of eligiblity remaining, will miss the rest of the season with a left shoulder injury, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-12T19:02:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50463373/sources-ole-miss-rb-kewan-lacy-miss-rest-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss RB Kewan Lacy out after dislocating shoulder","description":"Ole Miss running back Kewan Lacy suffered a dislocated shoulder in the Rebels' loss to Texas and has been ruled out for Saturday's game against Auburn.","published":"2026-10-26T18:17:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50288926/ole-miss-rb-kewan-lacy-dislocating-shoulder","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss to get star RB Kewan Lacy back vs. Vanderbilt","description":"Ole Miss star running back Kewan Lacy is expected to return for Saturday's game at Vanderbilt, coach Pete Golding said on Monday.","published":"2026-10-05T18:27:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50111069/ole-miss-get-star-rb-kewan-lacy-back-vs-vanderbilt","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss RB Kewan Lacy (shoulder) ruled out vs. Florida","description":"Kewan Lacy, the star running back for No. 4 Ole Miss, has been ruled out against No. 21 Florida on Saturday due to his left shoulder injury.","published":"2026-09-26T20:09:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50032888/ole-miss-rb-kewan-lacy-not-expected-play-vs-florida","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"RB Kewan Lacy not expected to be out long term, Golding says","description":"Ole Miss star running back Kewan Lacy will be a game-time decision for Saturday's game vs. Florida due to a shoulder injury, coach Pete Golding said on Monday.","published":"2026-09-21T17:43:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49995072/rb-kewan-lacy-not-expected-long-term-golding-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5086388/kewan-lacy","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kewan_Lacy"},"pick":{"pick":36,"round":2,"team":"NYJ","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Kewan Lacy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kewan_Lacy","description":"American football running back (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Kewan Duntrell Lacy (KEE-wahn; born July 6, 2006) is an American college football running back for the Ole Miss Rebels. He previously played for the Missouri Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Kewan Duntrell Lacy attended Fort Worth Nolan in Fort Worth, Texas, for his freshman and sophomore seasons. Despite only five carries as a freshman, Lacy exploded in his sophomore campaign, amassing 1,352 yards and 13 touchdowns on 135 carries. Eventually, he transferred to Lancaster High School in Lancaster, Texas. In Lacy's first season with the Tigers, his production was split with Arizona State University commit Kyson Brown. Lacy finished the season with 527 yards and 10 total touchdowns on 79 touches. In between seasons, he posted times of 10.79 and 10.81 in the 100 m dash As a senior, he rushed for 1,513 yards on 221 carries with 19 touchdowns. Despite earning 29 offers from schools such as Alabama, Ohio State, and Miami (FL), he committed to the University of Missouri to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his lone year at Missouri, his true freshman year in 2024, Lacy played in six games and rushed for 104 yards on 23 carries. After the season, he transferred to the University of Mississippi. In his first year at Ole Miss in 2025, he entered the season as the starting running back. Lacy rushed for 108 yards with three touchdowns in his first game. On November 8th, 2025 Lacy tied the Ole Miss single-season rushing touchdown record with 15."}]}}